#: ../../explanation/numerical_stability.md 629128d05c7048ada92c7832cf90ccc5
msgid ""
"Understand GWexpy numerical stability behavior, including whitening eps "
"handling, safe log plotting, NaN and Inf failure modes, and when users "
"should tune parameters."
msgstr ""
"GWexpy の数値安定性ガイドです。whiten の eps 処理、安全な対数表示、NaN / Inf の失敗モード、調整が必要な場面を整理します。"

#: ../../explanation/numerical_stability.md:7 1bf51f5011134472a53ecc2766e69439
msgid "Numerical Stability and Precision"
msgstr "数値的安定性と精度"

#: ../../explanation/numerical_stability.md:10
#: 26443cdffd0049019ed676a5c0e15b71
msgid ""
"**Who should read this page?** Standard analysis in `gwexpy` works out-of-"
"the-box with high stability. Refer to this detailed guide only if:"
msgstr ""
"**このページを読むべき方**: 通常の解析では `gwexpy` "
"のデフォルト設定で十分な安定性が確保されています。以下の状況に該当する場合のみ、この詳細ガイドを参照してください："

#: ../../explanation/numerical_stability.md:12
#: 44fbe533f3c24833857b6e4ec57bfcef
msgid ""
"You see \"holes\" or \"unusual colors\" in your plots caused by `NaN` or "
"`Inf`."
msgstr "プロット結果に `NaN` や `Inf` による「穴」や「異常な色」が現れた場合"

#: ../../explanation/numerical_stability.md:13
#: e7ad661d79a34d909d3669ab6cd70690
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"You are working with extremely small signals (below $10^{-23}$) or huge "
"signals (above 1) simultaneously."
msgstr "非常に微小な信号（$10^{-23}$以下）や、逆に 1 を超える巨大な信号を同時に扱う場合"

#: ../../explanation/numerical_stability.md:14
#: d0d92add1abe4e45b6883c163a89536d
msgid ""
"You want to deeply understand the numerical behavior of algorithms and tune "
"parameters like `eps` or `tol`."
msgstr "解析アルゴリズムの数値的な挙動を深く理解し、詳細パラメータ（`eps`, `tol`）を調整したい場合"

#: ../../explanation/numerical_stability.md:17
#: 5f495551df384d1d95294ede6d836dd9
msgid ""
"`gwexpy` is designed to handle data with an extremely wide dynamic range "
"without numerical breakdown."
msgstr ""
"`gwexpy` は、重力波データ解析で頻繁に扱われる極めて広いダイナミックレンジを持つデータを、数値的な破綻なく処理できるように設計されています。"

#: ../../explanation/numerical_stability.md:20
#: a7a18f5d0eec45049285593b60f56751
msgid "TL;DR"
msgstr "まず結論だけ知りたい方へ"

#: ../../explanation/numerical_stability.md:22
#: b3925d9a47ff49ffa40208a342c4f25e
msgid "For normal analysis, start by trusting the default `gwexpy` settings."
msgstr "通常の解析では、まず `gwexpy` のデフォルト設定をそのまま使ってください。"

#: ../../explanation/numerical_stability.md:23
#: 35b4e2f579134ffcb5226db128f20de1
msgid ""
"Do not add manual offsets such as `+ 1e-20` before plotting unless you have "
"a concrete reason."
msgstr "プロット前に `+ 1e-20` のような手動オフセットを足す必要はありません。"

#: ../../explanation/numerical_stability.md:24
#: bf6dcf19f7fe4c888b1e2d029cf52d29
msgid ""
"Tune parameters only when you actually observe `NaN` / `Inf`, work with "
"extreme amplitudes, or need algorithm-level validation."
msgstr "調整が必要なのは、`NaN` / `Inf` が見える、極端に小さい信号を扱う、アルゴリズム検証をしたい場合に限られます。"

#: ../../explanation/numerical_stability.md:27
#: 0daaf29afcad419f9dccde9dc88d93b0
msgid "Impact of Stabilization (Before & After)"
msgstr "可視化における安定化の効果 (Before & After)"

#: ../../explanation/numerical_stability.md:29
#: 74f08efbb2e246128f54d30394c7ea98
msgid ""
"A comparison between standard methods (simple `log10` or fixed `eps`) and "
"`gwexpy`'s robust numerical stabilization algorithms."
msgstr "標準的な手法（単純な `log10` や 固定 `eps`）と、`gwexpy` の数値安定化アルゴリズムを適用した結果の比較です。"

#: ../../explanation/numerical_stability.md:31
#: 0ff2d7167c3c41b7af50cf219376db5a
msgid ""
"![Numerical stabilization comparison: Noisy visualization with NaN/Inf "
"artifacts (Left) vs. Clean gravitational-wave signal "
"(Right)](../_static/images/numerical_stability_comparison.png)"
msgstr ""
"![数値安定化の比較：NaN/Inf "
"アーティファクトを含むノイズの多い可視化（左）と、クリーンな重力波信号（右）](../_static/images/numerical_stability_comparison.png)"

#: ../../explanation/numerical_stability.md:31
#: c4e620f11d784bf08d992d270f877810
msgid ""
"Numerical stabilization comparison: Noisy visualization with NaN/Inf "
"artifacts (Left) vs. Clean gravitational-wave signal (Right)"
msgstr "数値安定化の比較：NaN/Inf アーティファクトを含むノイズの多い可視化（左）と、クリーンな重力波信号（右）"

